{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Biographies", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Harry Houdini", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 15, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes effective texts in English showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shoeshine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who cleans and polishes shoes for a living", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: By the time he was eight years old, Ehrich was already selling newspapers and working as a shoeshine boy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a biography about a famous person.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "magic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the skill of performing tricks and illusions", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As a teenager in New York, Ehrich became interested in magic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "restraint", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that keeps a person immobile, such as a rope or a belt", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Today, when people hear the name Houdini, they think of the ability to escape from any restraint or difficult situation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to claim", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say that something is true", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Even today, people from Appleton claim that their city was Houdini's birthplace.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "card trick", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an illusion or deception performed with a deck of playing cards", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Calling himself Ehrich the Great, he began performing card tricks and other simple tricks for money.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "memoir", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a written account of someone's own life and experiences", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The book \"The Memoirs of Robert-Houdin\" was written by one of the world's greatest magicians.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "make a living", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to work; to earn money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He may have felt that this was another way of making a living.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le15ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research a magic trick.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write out a step-by-step procedure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I practice reading instructions out loud.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I narrate as I am performing an action.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and discover how to perform a simple magic trick.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write out the procedure, step by step.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the procedure out loud as you practice your trick.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Perform the trick for a partner. See if they can guess how it was done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Perform the trick again, this time explaining the procedure.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Passive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Sentences can be active or passive. Therefore, tenses also have \"active forms\" and \"passive forms.\"  </br> </br> In active sentences, the thing doing the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing receiving the action is the object. </br></br> In passive sentences, the thing receiving the action is the subject of the sentence and the thing doing the action is optionally included near the end of the sentence. You can use the passive form if you think that the thing receiving the action is more important or should be emphasized. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Object + was / were + past participle", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">The weather was affected by the unexpected cold currents.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Was / Were + object + past participle ... ?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">Was the weather affected by the cold currents?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ehrich was so influenced by what he read that he changed his name to Houdini. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When Houdini was four years old, he was taken to the United States by his parents.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "\"The Memoirs of Robert-Houdin\" was written by one of the world's greatest magicians. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Speculating About The Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We often guess about past situations based on what we know. You can choose modals based on how certain you are about your speculation. </br></br> When you are almost 100 percent certain that something was possible, use <span class=\"italic\">must have</span> or <span class=\"italic\">had to have</span>. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">must</span>  when we feel sure about something in the past. When you are less certain, use <span class=\"italic\">may have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might have</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>. We use <span class=\"strong\">might</span>, <span class=\"strong\">may</span> or <span class=\"strong\">could</span> to say that we think something was possible but we aren't sure. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"strong\">must have</span> + past participle</li><li> <span class=\"strong\">might have / might not have</span> + past participle</li><li> <span class=\"strong\">could have / couldn't have </span>+ past participle</li><li><span class=\"strong\"> may have / may not have </span>+ past participle </li> <li><span class=\"strong\">can't have </span>+ past participle</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "It must have been a challenging time for the family.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "His life could have been very different if his family had stayed in Europe.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He may have felt that this was another way of making a living.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Houdini might have wanted to hide his immigrant origins.", "type": "example"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can write about fame and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write about what was done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can speculate about the past in a written way.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Can you or anyone you know perform magic tricks? What kind?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What kind of personal qualities would you need to perform stunts and illusions?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"c